// GetAppRouteMetricsWithResponse Gets an app's routes
//
// Reads what an app served over a range ending now, from the rows the agent on each node writes
// from OBI (eBPF): every request its containers answered, from the proxy or from inside the
// project, by kind (http or rpc), method and route - a template such as /users/{id} when the
// app's framework names one. How many, how many failed (a 5xx, or an error), and p50, p95 and p99
// in milliseconds, close rather than exact: in totals, by route, and as series, one point per
// step, oldest first. `nodes` and `nodesCovered` count the nodes the app runs on now and those
// that run OBI. `available` is false, with a `reason`, when they cannot be read: the collection
// is off (performance-disabled) or off for the app (app-disabled), no node the app runs on runs
// OBI (node-disabled) or can (node-unsupported, with `preflightReasons`), the agent does not mark
// its lines yet (agent-unlabelled), or the logs cannot be read.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /projects/{projectID}/{projectEnv}/apps/{appID}/route-metrics (the `GetAppRouteMetrics` operationId).
